From 1116cfa07b8943ff9e792336e7ff54f1d1d79e72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:09:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/20] qwen3_5: a tower's static YaRN rope, as its config
 declares it

The HIP path read every checkpoint as plain rope and refused a scaled
one. SenseNova-Loop declares YaRN factor 2.0 over the trained 262,144
(a 524,288-position window), so the shared Spec now carries the rope
its config names: rope.zig resolves the tower's rope_parameters or
legacy rope_scaling, keeps plain rope within the trained window as
before, and builds the YaRN table transformers computes (the attention
factor, then 32 frequencies, from core/rope_yarn.zig) for a yarn block
whose factor and original window name the ceiling exactly. A block
with transformers' own defaults only: mscale, attention_factor, or a
non-default beta is refused, as the CUDA path's resolution refuses it.

The Metal 2B admission keeps its own rope rule; the standalone config
test module gains the core import rope.zig reads.
